Role Summary &amp; Impact &nbsp;

The Senior Associate,&nbsp; eCom/Digital Shopping plays a critical role in driving commerce performance through best-in-class product feed management, catalog optimization, and data strategy across search, social, and marketplace platforms. This role sits at the intersection of commerce, media, analytics, and technology, ensuring product data is accurate, optimized, and structured to maximize visibility, efficiency, and sales outcomes. &nbsp;

You will be responsible for managing and improving product feeds across platforms including Google Merchant Center, Microsoft Merchant Center, Meta Catalog Manager, and other feed-driven environments. Working closely with activation, analytics, client, and eCommerce teams, you'll identify opportunities to improve feed quality, automate processes, strengthen product segmentation, and unlock greater performance through data-driven insights and testing. &nbsp;

This is an ideal opportunity for someone with a strong foundation in commerce media, product feed management, analytics, and performance optimization who enjoys solving technical challenges and translating data into business impact. &nbsp;

What You'll Bring &nbsp;

• Experience in eCommerce, commerce media, feed management, shopping campaigns, or catalog operations. &nbsp;

• Strong analytical mindset with the ability to identify trends, opportunities, and performance drivers. &nbsp;

• Experience working with product feeds, catalog management platforms, and data governance processes. &nbsp;

• Familiarity with Google Merchant Center, Feedonomics, Meta Catalog Manager, SA360, or similar commerce technology platforms. &nbsp;

• Proven ability to collaborate across media, analytics, technology, and client teams to drive measurable business outcomes. &nbsp;

